{
  "$comment": "What the launcher's documents are held to: a knowledge base's, the stack's kinds (KnowledgeBase, KnowledgeIndex, Issuer, WorkerPool, Inference) and the project file `.semiont/config.yaml` (ProjectConfig, in ../kb-identity); and the Browser's (Browser), which belongs to no knowledge base. Each case names the schema it is read against and gives the document: `document`, YAML text, where YAML's own reading is the point or no fixture holds the kind; or `base`, a file of the launcher's fixture knowledge base, with `patch`, a JSON merge patch (RFC 7396) applied to it. `verdict` is `accepted`, or `refused` with `at`, the JSON pointer of the value refused, and `reason`: `unknown-field`, a field the schema does not name; `missing-required`; `wrong-type`; `not-allowed`, a value of the right type the schema refuses (a constant, a list, a pattern, a bound); or `exactly-one`, one of two ways to say a thing given both or neither. A runner reads each case against the schema it names, and fails on a verdict, `at` or `reason` other than the case's. A schema with no refused case is held to nothing.",
  "runBy": {
    "launcher": ["packages/go/launcher/stack/read_test.go"]
  },
